{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1531202-improved-cantrips-expanding-the-possibilities-of-the-cantrips-realm-based","id":1531202,"title":"Improved Cantrips: Expanding the Possibilities of the cantrips' realm-based","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-20T10:58:09-08:00","id":1531202,"title":"Improved Cantrips: Expanding the Possibilities of the cantrips' realm-based","content":"So hi, good morning from Brazil!<br /> <br /> I made some different things for changeling, i storytelling some years about the plot and I'm here to share some thoughts on the arts and realms in our role-playing game, and to propose a new, improved cantrip mechanic. I would love to hear what you have to say about this.<br /> <br /> Throughout our campaign, I have noticed some limitations and challenges regarding the arts and realms system. While they are fundamental to the gameplay experience, I feel that some of the abilities on offer may be a bit restrictive or not very versatile for a dream-driven narrative system. Additionally, progression within these systems can seem somewhat linear and predictable.<br /> <br /> To address these concerns, I'm proposing the introduction of improved cantrips. These cantrips would be advanced versions of the basic arts and realms, offering characters an alternative way as a new options and significant enhancements to their abilities. They could be unlocked through training, achievements, exploration, or even specific narrative events, adding an additional layer of progression and customization to characters. Much like the hedge magic system of sorcerers, improved cantrips always use Willpower with the dice pool at difficulty 8, but the realm influences this as a modifier below this same difficulty.<br /> <br /> So as I finish my book, you wi'll see:<br /> <br /> ORIGINAL CANTRIP - it's the C20 there.<br /> VARIANT CANTRIP - new cantrip as an alternative path to the linear progress and<br /> IMPROVED CANTRIP - based on static Dark Ages Fae cantrips, but here you use willpower permanent to execute it but you can't use Bunks and other additional Realms. As a numina, it does something and that's it.<br /> <br /> The Improved cantrip has a:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Activation Cost:</b> The player does not spend resources to use an improved cantrip, but is limited by his permanent Willpower level. This means they can use a limited amount of enhanced cantrips based on their Willpower.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Additional Effects: </b>Improved tricks have additional effects, always being considered fateful and affecting both the fairy world and the human world. However, in areas with high banality or in the Dreaming Realm, they may be less effective.<br /> <br /> <b>3. Improved Cantrip Types:</b><br /> Until now, there is 3 improved cantrip types:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Those that allow Changes to include more realms and <i>alter with </i>additional benefits to the original cantrip.</li> <li>Those changes to the faemien along with the desired art, with specific mechanics that can be acquired as &quot;Rights Owned&quot;.</li> <li>Enhancement of existing mundane skills, with no activation cost, but requiring XP for development.</li> <li>Tricks that function like spells, using the Changeling's Permanent Willpower to manifest static effects.</li> </ol>4. <b>Limitations:</b><ul><li>It is not possible to add more Realms than those indicated in the cantrip description.</li> <li>The player can cast these cantrips as many times as they want, but they run the risk of becoming Undone if they use too many tricks.</li> <li>Being Undone means forgetting the true fey essence, and may be confused with other races and supernatural classes. The Mists alter the true essence of fairies if they are migrating out of the Dreaming, not only in body, but also in soul.</li> </ul>for a clearer example see how it looked in the Spring art:<br /> <br /> <b>Spring \u2014 The Earth, grow, heal, bloom.</b><br /> ORIGINAL EFFECT (it's as it is in the C20 book, <i>nothing</i> changes here)<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Awaken anything inert.</li> <li>Grow vegetation over the target and spread everywhere from it</li> <li>Heal one level of bashing or lethal damage each turn/success.</li> <li>Create a circle that offers protection and concealment whether mundane or magical.</li> <li>True resurrection. The target is kept alive by Success/Scene.</li> </ol>VARIANT EFFECT (if you level up your Art, you are not obliged to follow the original, you can get a variant effect)<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>LV2 - Use nature and simulate the effects of primal 2-3 for the EARTH element only. (or WOOD if the player wish, but he chooses one only)</li> <li>LV4 - Use nature and simulate the effects of primal 4-5 only for the EARTH element, including its variants.</li> </ol>ENHANCED EFFECT (these spells only work this way, they are &quot;<i>ipsis litteris&quot;</i>, that means you <i>must</i> to follow exactly all the rules described and their limitations but, they are more potent in this sense)<ul><li><b>LV1 - Night Habits - </b>Use the Realm of Time and reduce the time needed to gain effects of night rest by hours per point.</li> <li><b>LV2 - Carnivorous -</b> creates a hedge of flexible trunks equipped with short, sharp thorns. Anyone trying to cross finds branches very tight and intertwined. The fence has a Strength score equal to the caster's Nature Realm, and they attempt to grab their opponents. Once the victim is entangled, the vines contract, viciously piercing the victim's flesh with the thorns (inflicting Nature + 1 lethal damage). If the target takes any damage, the true horror becomes apparent: the spikes suck blood at the rate of one level of damage per turn, until the victim is dead or your player generates two successes on a Strength + Athletics roll to break free. Three logs appear per success, within the trick area ( 6 ft by 2 ft).</li> <li><b>L</b><b>V2 - Wooden Arsenal - </b>The character with this cantrip is never unarmed, as long as he can touch anything made of wood. Branches of a tree turn into arrows in his hand, while a table leg turns into a club. The player rolls Prop. For the remainder of the scene, any source of wood he can touch turns into a melee weapon of his choice. Any weapon thus formed inflicts the usual damage for a weapon of this type, but all damage is considered lethal.</li> <li><b>LV3 - Immortal Tears:</b> If a target is healed, use Ator to heal yourself up to half efficiency, future attempts increase the difficulty.</li> <li><b>LV4 - Red Sap:</b> Per session, if you take damage, roll Stamina + Permanent Glamor. Every 2 successes gain 1 glamour, but never more than the total vitality lost. Even in human form the odor of his &quot;blood&quot; is a radar for creatures with supernatural sensitivity. By appealing to fate, your life-sustaining fluid possesses magical properties that are coveted as magical ingredients described in ancient forms of some tomes of hunters, sorcerers, and some lycanthropes, although you no longer produce blood while in fey form.</li> <li><b>LV4 - Help of the Forest: </b>This powerful trick summons trees from the earth to help. The player rolls Nature (difficulty 7). If successful, nearby trees (up to 20) lend the caster their assistance. The f\u00e9e must be specific as to the request; but if it is reasonable, the trees are obliged to help. They can, for example, help the fairy travel from one branch to another with ease, escaping her enemies. If a f\u00e9e hides among the branches, he gains two additional dice for any soak roll against bashing or lethal damage. Trees may be willing to attack the fairies' enemies. If this is the case, use the faith's Nature+Successes for an attack roll and determine the damage according to the size of the tree, from four to 12 dice. A large tall oak, for example, would do more damage than a young willow (although the willow can ensnare an enemy in its branches).</li> </ul>Some improved cantrips can permanently alter the appearance of the fairy, the fae-mien, but functioning as a passive ability or innate right, or as I here naming an acquired right.<br /> However, each art now has a tree of smaller skills that have variant and improved tricks.<br /> <br /> So a player who has 5 in a Realm could perform an Realm-based improved cantrip at difficulty 3, but Bunks cannot be used to further reduce the difficulty, as they are less effective in the dream realm. A cantrip that was made to work this way cannot be modified, as can the equally dramatic consequences of overusing these cantrips. This not only reflects a simpler mechanic of dealing with a dice pool for these cantrips, but also a clear description of the range of a cantrip.\u200b<br /> <br /> Some fellowships and fairy houses has some cantrips in that way, and there a mechanics as background Title and Remembrance to learn and use that improved cantrips. that was already made but I'm here to hear what you guys think about this idea(s).<br /> <br /> I'm really interested on your POV's.. Have you also felt that the arts and realms could be more dynamic and engaging? What kind of improved tricks would you like to see in our game? Your opinions and suggestions are critical to shaping the future of our campaign and ensuring everyone has a richer, more satisfying gaming experience.<br /> <br /> I intend to publish the final proposal, in the not so distant future, in the Vault and providing an opportunity for the community to discuss what they think about the proposal. It's valuable to have different perspectives as we continue to refine and develop our gaming systems. Between the sessions made here (going next to 20th session) the improved cantrip make his place, the characters stay more engaged with the cantrips and have more opportunities at his side, some arts who only work in a specific context or realm.. Please share your thoughts in the comments below.<br /> <br /> I look forward to hearing what you have to say and discussing ways to improve our skill system together.<br /> <br /> Thank you for your continued attention and <i>gentle</i> contribution.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28385,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28385-elderitch-unseelie","user":"Elderitch Unseelie","date":". 02-25-2024, 11:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28385-elderitch-unseelie","name":"Elderitch Unseelie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28385_1.png","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T02:10:45-08:00","id":1531501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderitch Unseelie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1531202-improved-cantrips-expanding-the-possibilities-of-the-cantrips-realm-based#post1531202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So hi, good morning from Brazil!<br /> <br /> I made some different things for changeling, i storytelling some years about the plot and I'm here to share some thoughts on the arts and realms in our role-playing game, and to propose a new, improved cantrip mechanic. I would love to hear what you have to say about this.<br /> <br /> Throughout our campaign, I have noticed some limitations and challenges regarding the arts and realms system. While they are fundamental to the gameplay experience, I feel that some of the abilities on offer may be a bit restrictive or not very versatile for a dream-driven narrative system. Additionally, progression within these systems can seem somewhat linear and predictable.<br /> <br /> To address these concerns, I'm proposing the introduction of improved cantrips. These cantrips would be advanced versions of the basic arts and realms, offering characters an alternative way as a new options and significant enhancements to their abilities. They could be unlocked through training, achievements, exploration, or even specific narrative events, adding an additional layer of progression and customization to characters. Much like the hedge magic system of sorcerers, improved cantrips always use Willpower with the dice pool at difficulty 8, but the realm influences this as a modifier below this same difficulty.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an interesting idea, and it does reflect a concern from CTD1e onwards. My main counterargument would be: why do we need variant and improved Arts if we already have Unleashing?<br /> <br /> In most cases, Unleashing does what this system does. It lets you bend the rules at a cost. It lets your creativity run riot. It's something with limited use; you can't spam Unleashings easily. Moreover, compared to this system, it's <b><i>really quite simple</i></b>.<br /> <br /> It may just be how they're written and laid out, but these current rules also seem overcomplicated to me. Where possible, you want a new system to use or mirror existing systems as much as possible. In this case, using the existing system for Arts is much better. You can always then add a limitation or exception if needed, but try to keep it simple (no more than one or two exceptions to the core rules).<br /> <br /> So, perhaps they work like normal cantrips, but you can't use Bunks with them or they always have to target the same Realm, because that's how you've learned them. That's it. They still use the same rules as other cantrips besides that.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> I would suggest reading the rules for Devotions in <i>Vampire: The Requiem 2e</i> and using those as a model for how to present variant Arts instead.<br /> <br /> You don't need separate systems for both variant and improved Arts; just combine them into a single system. Improved Arts would just be variant Arts with a prerequisite of the Art they &quot;improve&quot;.<br /> \u200b<br /> In Requiem, Devotions can be alternate powers for one level of a Discipline, or they can be the equivalent of combo Disciplines. Unlike in V5, however, Devotions don't replace the core Discipline powers; they're just unique abilities you develop alongside the core ability set.<br /> <br /> IMO, this is better than the V5 system of Disciplines, where you only get one power per dot, so have to skip some powers to take others. It's better for players, because they don't need as much system mastery, nor do they suffer from decision paralysis. They know that the core powers will cover the basics and there won't be any trap builds. Anything else they purchase is just a bonus on top of that, as it should be.<br /> <br /> It's also easier for the ST because you know two Gangrel with Protean 2 will have the same core abilities, but you can give them different Devotions to distinguish between them.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200bKeep variant Arts relatively cheap if you want people to have lots of them, thus increasing diversity between fae without having to strip them of the &quot;core&quot; powers in their Arts. Make them more expensive if you want them to be rarer.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> Alternatively, you can just rewrite the Arts to be more like Spheres. Maybe take a look at <i>Ars Magica</i>, since that informed the design of both Mage Spheres and Changeling Arts + Realms (they use a noun + verb system, so fire + create = create fire but fire + destroy = quench fire).<br /> <br /> Now, permanent or semi-permanent changes to the fae mien is where your proposal really shines. This is something unique and not something CTD really does yet. I would probably make these very costly compared to other variant Arts and tie them to a minimum Glamour rating. If your Glamour rating drops, you lose them.<br /> <br /> They might even be better handled as unique Merits that can only be gained through certain circumstances, with specific prerequisites, and they should probably have a long-term consequence -- e.g., you have to sacrifice a dot of Glamour permanently to manifest a very powerful enduring change, or you permanently mark a point of Willpower as imbalanced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T14:41:05-08:00","id":1531924,"title":"","content":"So hello, thank you very much for your response to the forum!<br /> <br /> First of all I feel honored to communicate with a representative of the LGBTQIA+ community and as part of the letter G community I feel happy to be communicating with you. Really very flattered and happy about it...<br /> <br /> Having said that, let's get to the points:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1531202-improved-cantrips-expanding-the-possibilities-of-the-cantrips-realm-based?p=1531501#post1531501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's an interesting idea, and it does reflect a concern from CTD1e onwards. My main counterargument would be: why do we need variant and improved Arts if we already have Unleashing?<br /> <br /> In most cases, Unleashing does what this system does. It lets you bend the rules at a cost. It lets your creativity run riot. It's something with limited use; you can't spam Unleashings easily. Moreover, compared to this system, it's really quite simple. .</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you very much again, my first point is that the Unleashing mechanic is very expensive for a changeling to execute and narratively to me it sounds like an ex-machina (a narrative resource to continue the story without much explanation), and paying due price, 2 glamor points and receive 1 nightmare die, you can do what you need while keeping the verbs that a certain art controls, and Unleashing must be devastating, unprecedented with gigantic and exaggerated proportions as you will be forcing a flow that has no control. But while the Changeling could learn static sorcery being effective on both sides, then supposing the fae would use his willpower to use sorcery he would use the closest knowledge he has to what is mundane or historically known as autumnal, which in this case would be the Realms.<br /> <br /> Considering that sorcerer magic uses willpower at difficulty 8 as the standard dice pool, the closest parallel we find in the Realms as a difficulty modifier to reflect an understanding of how the fae system works, even in modern times is difficult to fit glamor in a line of human understanding. In this way, the Realm does not function as a passive force that only works by combining the Arts as before, but as an understanding of how reality works in modern times by human standards, being effective in the uses of tricks that are adapted to operate on earth.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1531202-improved-cantrips-expanding-the-possibilities-of-the-cantrips-realm-based?p=1531501#post1531501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b It may just be how they're written and laid out, but these current rules also seem overcomplicated to me. Where possible, you want a new system to use or mirror existing systems as much as possible. In this case, using the existing system for Arts is much better. You can always then add a limitation or exception if needed, but try to keep it simple (no more than one or two exceptions to the core rules).<br /> <br /> So, perhaps they work like normal cantrips, but you can't use Bunks with them or they always have to target the same Realm, because that's how you've learned them. That's it. They still use the same rules as other cantrips besides that.<br /> <br /> <br /> I would suggest reading the rules for Devotions in Vampire: The Requiem 2e and using those as a model for how to present variant Arts instead.<br /> <br /> You don't need separate systems for both variant and improved Arts; just combine them into a single system. Improved Arts would just be variant Arts with a prerequisite of the Art they &quot;improve&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> I haven't played a vampire, I don't have that much experience to talk about how it would work, perhaps based on the proposal he suggests, but my second point is that fairies, in the Dark Ages, you could do magic in two ways: using the power of glamour( there they call it Mists) and using the power of &quot;banality&quot; (which they call it Weavering) with the power of the Mists, you can change your fae mien, unleash, enchant mortals, etc.. and with the power of the weaver you can use the cantrips that exist there. In a quick read of the Domains chapter, you'll see that many cantrips that exist in the second and first edition exist in the Dark Ages, with their power significantly reduced in the 20th Anniversary Edition... my concern, in bringing this back to the modern world, without offending the community consensus, is to make the changeling a true hybrid in its dimensions, dealing as a concept-spirit being with a human form.<br /> <br /> With another example, see the difference in power scaling between a variant cantrip and an enhanced cantrip:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> LV3 - Mekamorphosis - Choose an object to merge with the Authority, the now merged objects function interdependently and can develop new purposes for the same function. The player must specify to the Narrator what the fused item can do.\u200b </div> </div> </div> Note that I am not limiting what will be merged but regardless of what it is, it will always be an object. So I could have drones embedded in an animal or plant, metal plates on another person and even energy cannons on my own arms. Unlike the cantrip below which works very specifically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> LV3 - Material Possession - Test Prop and convert a non-living, non-magical object into a tattoo on the f\u00e9e's body. The tattoo can be removed from the face using this trick. In case of need, a f\u00e9e can also hide itself in a certain object by fusing its essence with the material, although the f\u00e9e is limited to the material physical capabilities of the object, no one through mundane means can detect it, except for a supernatural being, including changelings, who beat him in successes on difficulty 9. Needless to say (or not) that there are no known changelings who failed this trick, just disappeared.\u200b </div> </div> </div> Here you can specifically store mundane materials only in your own body but do not use them, your mundane and faerie body would reflect these tattoos on your body, but this metamorphosis aims to guard objects, just as only you could hide in mundane objects. Here it is very effective for a single direction, while the variant trick above is a generic one made to work across multiple realms. This makes things a little more balanced by comparing the magical systems of other supernatural races like wizards and werewolves themselves.\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> But, you gave me a very interesting suggestion! I can propose to a changeling who wanted to simulate a cantrip in the spellbook I'm creating that already exists and he didn't buy that he tries to unleashed &quot;in a controlled manner&quot; so you would spend a glamour point so that you have access to a cantrip that you didn't buy when the goal is to do exactly what that trick does. If you fail, you fail critically(a botch), if you win, your successes are exceptional regardless how many success or fails you got it. This is also possible in Fae, Dark Ages, but you don't pay for it there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1531202-improved-cantrips-expanding-the-possibilities-of-the-cantrips-realm-based?p=1531501#post1531501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> In Requiem, Devotions can be alternate powers for one level of a Discipline, or they can be the equivalent of combo Disciplines. Unlike in V5, however, Devotions don't replace the core Discipline powers; they're just unique abilities you develop alongside the core ability set.<br /> <br /> IMO, this is better than the V5 system of Disciplines, where you only get one power per dot, so have to skip some powers to take others. It's better for players, because they don't need as much system mastery, nor do they suffer from decision paralysis. They know that the core powers will cover the basics and there won't be any trap builds. Anything else they purchase is just a bonus on top of that, as it should be.<br /> <br /> It's also easier for the ST because you know two Gangrel with Protean 2 will have the same core abilities, but you can give them different Devotions to distinguish between them.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200bKeep variant Arts relatively cheap if you want people to have lots of them, thus increasing diversity between fae without having to strip them of the &quot;core&quot; powers in their Arts. Make them more expensive if you want them to be rarer.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b<br /> Alternatively, you can just rewrite the Arts to be more like Spheres. Maybe take a look at Ars Magica, since that informed the design of both Mage Spheres and Changeling Arts + Realms (they use a noun + verb system, so fire + create = create fire but fire + destroy = quench fire).</div> </div> </div> </div>Here you arrived exactly as I narrate the magical system before this new proposal. Personally, I find the communication written of this specific plot very subjective, giving free rein to the imagination, but this leaves the Narrator with a loose end that he is not always prepared to deal with. Therefore, as humans and therefore agents of the weaver, we need to define a limit so that the changeling can exceed this limit whenever they wish and want (considering its appropriate consequences). And to create these tricks I am evoking what exists in Ars Magica. So, as you already well explained, combining the Arts that exist and their verbs there is in the anniversary edition and understanding the Realms as nouns, gives rise to a variety of tricks that work specifically for that Realm. I'm so happy and excited that I didn't need to talk about Ars Magica and we reached the same core of the game design system proposal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1531202-improved-cantrips-expanding-the-possibilities-of-the-cantrips-realm-based?p=1531501#post1531501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> <br /> Now, permanent or semi-permanent changes to the fae mien is where your proposal really shines. This is something unique and not something CTD really does yet. I would probably make these very costly compared to other variant Arts and tie them to a minimum Glamour rating. If your Glamour rating drops, you lose them.<br /> <br /> They might even be better handled as unique Merits that can only be gained through certain circumstances, with specific prerequisites, and they should probably have a long-term consequence -- e.g., you have to sacrifice a dot of Glamour permanently to manifest a very powerful enduring change, or you permanently mark a point of Willpower as imbalanced.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lastly and most impactfully, built-in passive abilities, such as birthrights, not only influence your fae-mien and your fey composition, as we call voile, but reflect the advancement of your studies in the art, giving you the opportunity to explore effects. that fit into that art but were not officially discussed. I'm going to consider what you said because it's very interesting and fits with what Lost sets out to do by making a changeling more part-fae than part-human.<br /> <br /> <br /> Considering that I'm giving you the option to convert metamorphosis (from animal transformation) to mekamorphosis (from cyber-fae transformation), this would be an improved trick available at level 4 that converts your fae mien into a machine part (birthright consulted from the Foul and Fair supplement, from the dark ages):\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> LV4 - Mekatronic Ascension -<br /> <br /> Seeming Improved: Sometimes a rare fae appears to be a complex automaton, whether due to so many fae implants or her automotive chrysalis. Whether it's made of a clock, springs or steam-powered pistons, even integrated circuits and/or digitalized parts, Dreaming doesn't make any distinction when he wants to call someone his son/and. Although they appear to have an artificial build, they are, in all other respects, perfectly normal fairies and can reproduce with other Fairies. Their minds powered by precise circuits and alchemical chips grant a +1 bonus to Intelligence, an absorption of +2B / +2L and they can rearrange their limbs into any tool, in a Willpower test using Accessory. This semblance also allows you to work in many real-world situations, and other Nockers envy you, although they also find your condition somewhat suspicious. This effect is essentially the same as Iron Resistance (see Changeling: The Dreaming second edition); however, not only are you immune to iron, but your chimeric works are equally resistant. On the other hand, you lose the ability to heal yourself naturally. Lost health levels must be repaired with an extended Intelligence + Crafts roll (difficulty equal to 3+ the number of health levels lost), each test taking up half a day's work. Any magical effect on your body must be done using the Realm Prop. You can still heal yourself to human patterns by evoking Autumn.\u200b </div> </div> </div> Here you still maintain your birthright independent of kith, but you have a mechanized cyber-fae form, such as a mechanical fox pooka or a redcap that looks like an industrial furnace or a millimetrically blueprinted drawled beautiful sidhe dougal.<br /> Again, I'm more than honored to respond. I'm almost at the end of the book, which is close to 100 pages and 20 narrated sessions. It certainly has more than 200 improved and alternative tricks alongside the original tricks. It's a lot of work to diagram all of this hehe.<br /> <br /> Thank you very much! DREAM!\u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28385-elderitch-unseelie","name":"Elderitch Unseelie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28385_1.png","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T22:15:11-07:00","id":1532543,"title":"","content":"Ah, I found that book Dark Ages Fae and I immediately fell in love to it, a pity it is basically nothing like Changeling the Dreaming at all... And while I love both, I gotta say that the powers of the Dark Ages Fae were far better than the &quot;Discipline-like&quot; style of CtD.<br /> <br /> I also loved both ideas about the Fae - both as &quot;Dream beings&quot; fighting to bring Glamour back to the world against its Banality, and the Fae that are creatures born out of the Mists, beings of primordial magic. Fascinating concepts for both.<br /> <br /> And yes, I would very much prefer to have the Changelings from CtD to use the same system for their &quot;magic&quot; as it was in Dark Ages Fae... And I would also want more content related to Dark Ages Fae.. Even if that were turned into a completely new splat...<br /> <br /> Oh, by the way, I'm also from Brasil my brother. I'm from the city of Santos/SP, a pleasure to meet you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T22:32:57-07:00","id":1532545,"title":"","content":"Ok, so I see you're also a fan of Fae Dark Ages. Ok, it's important to notice that Fae Dark Ages, although I consider it a true master piece, has largely been forgotten by White Wolf, and I'm not even sure that the OP knows that they own this title under their IP. I'm fairly sure they have no idea that it exists.<br /> <br /> So, the only ever book printed about them was... Dark Ages Fae.<br /> <br /> And you and I are probably amongst the few people who ever knew that this book existed, besides the writers and publishers (maybe). Which is an absolute shame, but it is what it is.<br /> <br /> And they have absolutely nothing to do with the Changelings from Changeling the Dream. Nothing. Zero. You could very well consider them to be two different games from 2 different splats, just like the Changelings are not Werewolves nor vampires.<br /> <br /> That being said, the &quot;Mists&quot; are NOT &quot;Glamour&quot; and neither the &quot;Weaver&quot; is Banality, although they have some resemblance. They remain however as fundamentally distinct concepts.<br /> <br /> Now, the powers of the Dark Ages Fae, they are vastly superior to the system in Changeling the Dream, and I don't mean in terms of &quot;look at my awesome superpowers&quot; (although they are), but rather in terms of mechanics.<br /> <br /> I would rather use the mechanics of Dark Ages Fae as they are, rather than trying an amalgamation between the two games. I think Changeling the Dream would become vastly improved by using the system from DA:Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-15T18:56:49-07:00","id":1532677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1531202-improved-cantrips-expanding-the-possibilities-of-the-cantrips-realm-based?p=1532545#post1532545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so I see you're also a fan of Fae Dark Ages. Ok, it's important to notice that Fae Dark Ages, although I consider it a true master piece, has largely been forgotten by White Wolf, and I'm not even sure that the OP knows that they own this title under their IP. I'm fairly sure they have no idea that it exists.<br /> <br /> So, the only ever book printed about them was... Dark Ages Fae.<br /> <br /> And you and I are probably amongst the few people who ever knew that this book existed, besides the writers and publishers (maybe). Which is an absolute shame, but it is what it is.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm right there with you both. Probably my very favorite book from the original World of Darkness line.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1531202-improved-cantrips-expanding-the-possibilities-of-the-cantrips-realm-based?p=1532545#post1532545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And they have absolutely nothing to do with the Changelings from Changeling the Dream. Nothing. Zero. You could very well consider them to be two different games from 2 different splats, just like the Changelings are not Werewolves nor vampires.<br /> <br /> That being said, the &quot;Mists&quot; are NOT &quot;Glamour&quot; and neither the &quot;Weaver&quot; is Banality, although they have some resemblance. They remain however as fundamentally distinct concepts.<br /> <br /> Now, the powers of the Dark Ages Fae, they are vastly superior to the system in Changeling the Dream, and I don't mean in terms of &quot;look at my awesome superpowers&quot; (although they are), but rather in terms of mechanics.<br /> <br /> I would rather use the mechanics of Dark Ages Fae as they are, rather than trying an amalgamation between the two games. I think Changeling the Dream would become vastly improved by using the system from DA:Fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't *quite* agree. They're more like the relationship between the modern and Dark Ages versions of Mage - creatures that so intimately connected to the zeitgeist of their Age and so very different eras result in very different outcomes. I don't think Dark Ages Fae would work any better in modern day than Changelings would work in the Dark Ages.<br /> <br /> The lore continuity, I think, is instructive. Dark Ages Changelings are human/fae hybrids. Modern Changelings are Dark Ages Firstborn who have been reborn into human bodies, as a last desperate ploy to survive the end of the Mythic Age. Where modern fae fear banality overwhelming their Fae side with their human one, the (literally) godlike Fae of the Mythic Age feared Echoes - sharp-edged beliefs.<br /> <br /> All that is to say, I think it would be more interesting to walk that forward - take the Dark Ages system of mythic god-powers and think about how they would change if the Firstborn were forced to continuously reincarnate in human bodies that shield them from echoes but make them vulnerable to Banality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 03-16-2024, 02:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-20T20:06:04-07:00","id":1536030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1531202-improved-cantrips-expanding-the-possibilities-of-the-cantrips-realm-based?p=1532545#post1532545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so I see you're also a fan of Fae Dark Ages. Ok, it's important to notice that Fae Dark Ages, although I consider it a true master piece, has largely been forgotten by White Wolf, and I'm not even sure that the OP knows that they own this title under their IP. I'm fairly sure they have no idea that it exists.<br /> <br /> So, the only ever book printed about them was... Dark Ages Fae.<br /> <br /> And you and I are probably amongst the few people who ever knew that this book existed, besides the writers and publishers (maybe). Which is an absolute shame, but it is what it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually DA Fae is well known, and does have a number of fans.<br /> <br /> The reason it has never been worked on again has more to do precisely with your perception that it is another creature entirely.<br /> <br /> It was meant to be the actual past of the Changelings, but at the end it became irreconcilable with Dreaming and with the WoD in general, even other DA lines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":". 05-20-2024, 11:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-26T09:30:08-07:00","id":1536305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1531202-improved-cantrips-expanding-the-possibilities-of-the-cantrips-realm-based?p=1536030#post1536030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually DA Fae is well known, and does have a number of fans.<br /> <br /> The reason it has never been worked on again has more to do precisely with your perception that it is another creature entirely.<br /> <br /> It was meant to be the actual past of the Changelings, but at the end it became irreconcilable with Dreaming and with the WoD in general, even other DA lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a shame regardless. I wouldn't mind having more material for it, even if it became its own thing, even outside of WoD itself","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-26T10:34:11-07:00","id":1536308,"title":"","content":"You're not the only one, but unfortunately I don't think it will happen. By C20 (an excellent work) it's kind of confirmed that medieval fae just followed similar rules to modern ones.<br /> <br /> There's even a class of fey that do not rely on human bodies at all, and is easy to extrapolate to the others so we have a sense of what pre-changeling Kithain would look like.<br /> <br /> Other than that, for this thread I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5291_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5291\" data-vbnamecard=\"5291\">adambeyoncelowe</a> said it all. Unleashing does most of the work in C20, and other than that, Requiem's Devotions do exactly the same work <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28385-elderitch-unseelie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar28385_1.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28385\" data-vbnamecard=\"28385\">Elderitch Unseelie</a> is doing, but with simpler rules.<br /> <br /> Basically, a Devotion is a separate power with relatively low cost, but with specific dots in Disciplines as prerequisites. It may be an alternative power to that level, a combination of Disciplines, or an enhancement to its prerequisites, so it literally covers the same bases as this system here.<br /> <br /> If making those extra powers more constrained is so important to the system, those &quot;Iconic Cantrips&quot; could be locked to the Realms used as prerequisites, but be cheaper.<br /> <br /> Let's say you want the power to give your retainers a move bonus from any distance. It could have as prerequisites Naming 2, Hopscotch 2, Actor 2. Actor doesn't count for the XP cost, so you end up with a power that costs 2 XP to learn, but it only affects Actors and can't be modified with any other Realm. It gives a bonus based on Hopscotch 2, but to movement in general, to a named target.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-19T06:38:04-08:00","id":1547829,"title":"","content":"Hello guys, first of all, happy new year! I hope you had a good time, with those I would like to spend!<br /> Secondly, I still maintain the pertinent changes, especially with regard to the magic system, which is clear that some are much less powerful/versatile than the others, I am advancing a lot with several training sessions and table tests among my friends in Brazil, reaching almost 200 pages of raw text with some test campaigns for narrators to test their customizations. I didn't have the experience of playing with Vampire, fortunately all my reference is based on test sessions in the Dark Ages, Fae (DAF) and I'm happier for that.<br /> <br /> My main complaint is still in the transition between paradigms of magical systems, things that I was writing with some translators from my country for a possible Companion DAF.<br /> <br /> To the variant cantrips, I will not require another art as a prerequisite, I still believe that the cost is too high for learning, to get arts that no longer work very well in what was planned and get something very little because of that em compara\u00e7ao com outros Plots of the same plot, dreams should be broad, greater, less plastered. But some arts necessarily need to be more effective by what they originally propose to do. For this, I went to the second edition and set up an art tree based on the domains where it is possible to find the parallels without torturing any data because of it.<br /> <br /> In short, I will stick to the document with the following changes, according to what the wonderful book DAF does. But respecting what the canon written in C20.<br /> <br /> <b>Plot Modifications</b><br /> <br /> I won't lie to you, creating systems is cool, let's face it, to be able to say that our impression is registered and marked with ideas and thoughts that are so wonderful (for us) that we soon want others to see the potential of our creations. But we can't always count on the other to understand or fully agree with our ideas and aspirations. For this, a common basis must be agreed, respected so that everyone can be in the same thought, especially players and narrators.<br /> <br /> And for that, for those who need it, some rules need to be clear about what is being added...<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>To the Birthright</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Some tricks permanently affect the face of the fairy, this is not only an evolution of her knowledge in this specific art but, to the Nouns (im the arts) with which the fairy wants to adhere not only in body but also in her true being, her soul. This statistic directly reflects the mechanics of DAF that by evolving its score in mists new aspects are unlocked. All changelings start with their Birthright intact as in the C20 system, some arts have improved tricks that are permanently attached to the fairy's seeming. Called Acquired Right, it begins to act as a modifier of some skills and offering new features that can be adherent to its form. I didn't establish the minimum of Permanent Glamour, which is a mechanic that even belongs to DA, what would break what was described in the c20 about the Kiths, so I'm establishing that this is a possible evolution of the art that changeling is studying to improve.<br /> Example:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Acquired rights that are based on permanent glamour. </b>Skycraft - LV1 - Change of Seeming: The fairies who start in this Art discover that they develop a strange lightness in the countenance; they seem to float just a few centimeters above the ground, with shadows and clouds follow the character, rotating around him in a whirlwind of light, darkness and steam. From time to time, small thunder orbs dance over his body, generating small rays that seem to exchange with the earth so that he never deigns to dirty his feet on it. This also makes your hair and clothes wave strangely with a ghostly and electrifying breeze. For each target successfully electrified in this scene, receive an electric charge, it is a small chimerical sphere that orbits you in harmony with other spheres of energy generated by this art, you can store up to the limit of your permanent glamour and you can use one of these charges to simulate the effects of Spring 1 only on electrical devices or modify your unarmed attack to +2.</li> <li><b>Acquired rights that change the physical form of the fairy (but not your Kith). </b>Metamorphosis - LV3 - Change of Seeming: Some aspects of your animal countenance are transferred to your fairy face. This may mean that you have preensile feet or tail, ability to climb vertical surfaces, sticky tongue, rotating eyes 180 degrees, extra legs, scorpion stinger, poisonous bite, hard skin, skunk spray or any of a huge variety of unique attributes that affinities can have.</li> </ol></li> </ol></li> </ol><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>When Unleashing</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>I was worried as well as the author of the DAF book about the abuse of Unleashed mechanics, which in dark ages is much simpler. You can emulate an improved cantrips <i>Unleashed Controllably,</i> as long as you execute following all your rules and expenses, this is <i>Ipsis litteris</i>, the cantrips that change your fairy seeming are not included, your successes count for the effectiveness of the trick but they cannot exceed the total dots you have in Art, if this happens the effects happen but in a way distorted to the intention. Statistically speaking, you don't spend willpower to perform this effect, but a glamour point is required for each attempt. When it unties, trying to achieve an improved cantrip, its surplus successes from a failure are considered critical failures and are converted into glamour.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><i>Optional Mechanics:</i> Unleashed Controlled requires knowledge, you can't Unleashed cantrips that are above your permanent level of fae level. Consiting if greymare is an alternative, but I don't like to leave statistics dependent on skills from the standard pattern dice pool.</li> </ol></li> </ol></li> <li><b>When Evoking Autumn</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>This is really the new part of the mechanics that separates the dark ages of modern changeling, a clear and explicit mechanic of what happens when a changeling abuses its &quot;static cantrips&quot;.I start from the beginning, as it is written in the Dark Ages that all the changelings are already &quot;Locked&quot;, with comparison to what they were in the previous periods, here I reinforce this statistic penalizing for the excessive execution of static cantrips in the same Scene of the game session. A locked changeling is taking off his fairy soul to other prodigious forms. This Progression is slow but part of the creative principle of the power of the Mists affects without restriction to everything it creates, especially the changelings who in this condition behave like natives in an otherwise prodigious way, having with them some qualities such as Fairy Blood and/or Affinity with fairies but will not take anything with them from Dreaming, including their Treasures, Chimeras, Castles, Titles and Arts, except for the improved cantrips and score in Realms in equivalence.</li> </ol></li> <li><b>Invoke the Wyrd, Travel in the Dreaming</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Improved cantrips are much more difficult to control when you are using the power of Dreams, both in fairy form or in the plane of dreams. By bringing the dream with you in its true essence, the worldly must be left behind, and wherever the organ capable of processing information is now, it is too chaotic to conceive the worldly reality in its literality, at the cost of taking off to Dream power.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><i>Optional Mechanics: </i>The Background of Remembrance can decrease, in one step per point, the difficulty of launching an improved trick while appealing to Dreaming/Wyrd.</li> </ol></li> </ol></li> <li><b>Fae Houses, Titles, and some secrets..</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The fairy courts have pasts and stories about the foundations of reality itself in a very individualized way, each one focused on a specific theme, be it faith, aristocracy, poetry, discoveries, war and inventions. It would not be difficult to imagine that your own improved cantrip was developed by a specific house. Below is a main theme of the house, if you want to attribute a cantrip to it, as a suggestion, follow the Arts Associated with noble houses, where each society (subgroups) has a prominent art.</li> </ol></li> <li><b>To the cantrips</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>To the variant cantrips, I will not require another art as a prerequisite, I still believe that the cost is too high for learning, to get arts that no longer work very well in what was planned and get something very little because of that Compared to other Plots of the same plot, dreams should be broad, greater, less plastered. But some arts necessarily need to be more effective by what they originally propose to do. For this, I went to the second edition and set up an Art Tree based on the Domains where it is possible to find the parallels without torturing any data source because of it. Exemple: you want a fire sword but you have Summer instead Primal, with level 2 I allow you to buy the cantrip variation to create fire as primal 2, but only for fire element (because in the DAF Summer is domain of Fire).<br /> The improved effects are specific versions of cantrips of a given Art, adjusted to perform more focused and powerful functions. Unlike the original (I like them or not (probably not)) or variants, they follow fixed statistics described and have less versatility. For the purpose of this book, there are four types of improved tricks:<ul><li><i>Change of Original Cantrips: </i>Allow you to include more realms or specific benefits in an existing trick. Example: In Skyscraper, the Level 4 trick, Grandfather Thunder Touch, directly changes the Original Cantrip giving lethal power to the rays and allowing the execution of specific improved cantrips.</li> <li><i>Change of Seeming:</i> Permanently change the seeming of the changeling, adding innate skills or modifying its physical form. These changes follow specific mechanics and can be acquired as <i>Acquired Rights, in</i> opposition to the Birthrights where you defined the kith when you created the character, these powers reveal your mastery by doubling your fairy form. Example: A Nocker with the Seeming of Metamorphosis would have a team of birds always willing to cooperate; A Nocker with the Forged for War Seeming (from the Art of the Dragon's Ire) has a rigid appearance and has claws that cause lethal damage.</li> <li>Improvement of Existing Skills: Improve an already known skill without activation cost. These tricks act as a permanently active Birth right, without the need for additional tests. Example: a chasing police Sidhe could use Aggressive Driving of Dragon Ire to destroy the vehicle of his aggressors.</li> <li>Those that function as passive skills: While some tricks directly affect the scene and require a statement from the player to be active, others do not need to and act on the described conditions of the trick. Example: A Boggan who uses the art of Legerdemain several times can activate Tactile Telekinesis, a passive cantrip who saves 1 dice when you cast any cantrip in that Art in the scene to trigger a some of effects telekinesis-based.</li> </ul></li> </ol></li> </ol><br /> <b>I needed to strongly nerf the Fae Realm in the magical system</b>, despite understanding the historical context of the Shattering' period (something I'm building for the FAE Companion book) and the rupture of spiritual powers, I removed as optional mechanics completely the domain of fairies, so things are as they are, Actors, regardless of where they are actors, trees are trees, ephemeral who behave like animals, are affected by Nature, magical objects are still objects.<br /> <br /> So, if a changeling is building a &quot;career&quot; of cantrips aimed at a specific Art, as a Storyteller I grant to you a option to a an elevation of power to the fairy who is working for it. The marking below is a suggestion for changelings who wanted their spells to become more lethal due to the continuous practice of their efforts. Continuous practice and mastery of a specific Art allow changelings to perfect their cantrips, raising them to levels of sophistication and power beyond the conventional. Through the application of Meta-Magic, players can customize and improve their tricks, reflecting progressive magical learning and specialization over time.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b><br /> For independent cantrips, I'm according to what they are proposing for the fifth editions (I liking them or not) but the recommended is the Permanent Glamour, as well as I would change in DAF as permanent score Mists for the total dices. By creating a campaign I am allowing the ST assigned to the cantrips to:<ul><li>Decrease the standard difficulty (usually 8). Or</li> <li>Be added to the dice pool, depending on the Narrator.</li> </ul><b>Test Rules:</b><ul><li><b>Realms Reigning over Glamour:</b><ul><li>The default difficulty is 8, but the Realm can reduce the difficulty based on your level. Example: If the cantrip uses Scene and the character has Scene 3, the difficulty drops to 5.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Add Everything in the Pool dices:</b><ul><li>Alternatively, as in the fifth editions are doing, I like them or not, Realms can add to the pool, maintaining the standard difficulty (8). Example: A cantrips that uses Time, adds Time Realm to Permanent Glamour to maximize successes, in that way, you can have 15 dices in your total pools.</li> </ul></li> </ul>My friends and I are excited about the changes we are creating here, I tried to contact the Pooka G to talk about these changes because they are apparently following the same path, I'd rather add strength than diverge, building bridges I think necessary. Better news will come. Dream!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28385,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28385-elderitch-unseelie","user":"Elderitch Unseelie","date":"English is not my first language, everything I learned was based on final fantasy) 01-22-2025, 05:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28385-elderitch-unseelie","name":"Elderitch Unseelie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28385_1.png","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}